mechanical-retirement rates between constructors, and `name` lets us report the answer with readable team names.\n\n4) **nationality** is written as an adjective (\"British\"), while circuits used country names (\"UK\"). Question 2 is about the driver's home country, not the team's, so this column is not needed.\n\n5) **Available before the race?** Yes. Which team a constructor is does not change during a race, so nothing in this table is leakage. `constructorRef` and `url` are descriptive and not needed for any of our questions.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**Do renamed teams really get new IDs?** The F1 introduction gives one team's history as an example: Toleman became Benetton, then Renault, Lotus and Alpine. We look up these names to see how the table records them.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"df = raw[\"constructors\"]\ndf[df[\"name\"].str.contains(\"Toleman|Benetton|Renault|Lotus|Alpine\")][[\"constructorId\", \"constructorRef\", \"name\"]]","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-16T15:34:36.317577Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-16T15:34:36.317917Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-16T15:34:36.339087Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-16T15:34:36.317887Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-16T15:34:36.33813Z"}},"outputs":[{"execution_count":6,"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":"     constructorId  constructorRef                       name\n3                4         renault                    Renault\n21              22        benetton                   Benetton\n31              32      team_lotus                 Team Lotus\n51              53         toleman                    Toleman\n169            172    lotus-climax               Lotus-Climax\n170            173  lotus-maserati             Lotus-Maserati\n173            176       lotus-brm                  Lotus-BRM\n174            177  lotus-borgward             Lotus-Borgward\n177            180      lotus-ford        